Let me begin by saying that this is my first post here, or, indeed, on
any newsgroup, so I apologize if I actually "toppost" or commit any
other slanderous act that would cause me to be sacrificed to Moloch.

I play NetHack because, out of all the games I've played, it never
gets boring. There's no one way to go about doing things, indeed, if I
try to play each game the same way, I die. There's always something
new to find, even for a player who's been spoiled as absolutely rotten
as I have. The challenge is another major part of it, also. With most
games out today it's just assumed that you'll eventually get to the
end, even if you're a six year old with Fetal Alcohol Syndrome. (No
offense is intended to anyone with or anyone who knows someone with
FAS. In fact, one of my good friends, and one of the best gamers I
know, has it.) My point is that getting to the end of NH and actually
beating it is a huge accomplishment, one that I hope to one day
achieve.

I personally don't play on servers because I can't stand having people
watch me play. It really is as simple as that.

As for rgrn, I mostly lurk here because a) I'm not the kind of person
who asks questions, b) I don't really feel qualified to give advice,
and c) well, really, there is no c, but any decent list needs three
parts to it.

